# Own-wording spells of Dark Matter (2014 rules), part C.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Mega Image": ["10,000 ft, Concentration. A convincing image up to a 1,000 ft cube that fools sensors.",
 "10,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You create the image of an object, creature or other visible phenomenon no larger than a 1,000-ft cube, at a spot you see in range. It seems completely real, with fitting sounds, smells, temperatures and cosmic signals. It cannot make enough heat or cold to hurt, a sound loud enough to deal Thunder damage or deafen, or a smell that sickens. While you are in range, you can use your action to move it to another spot in range, changing its look so the movement seems natural. For example, an asteroid can rotate. You can also vary its sounds over time. Touching it reveals an illusion, since objects pass through. It does fool sensor systems. A creature that uses its action to examine it can spot the illusion with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. A creature that sees through it finds its other sensory qualities faint."],
"Memorize": ["Touch. Remember a page of text exactly for a year, then recall it with Advantage.",
 "Touch. A page of written text and a silver string worth 10 gp, tied in a knot, are consumed. As you cast, your eyes pass over the words and commit them to memory. For the next year you remember all the information on the page exactly. After that, you have Advantage on Intelligence checks to recall it."],
"Meteoroid Shower": ["10,000 ft. 1,000 ft radius burst. Dexterity save or 8d6 mega Bludgeoning.",
 "10,000 ft. You create a barrage of asteroids at a point in range. Mega creatures and the pilots of ships in a 1,000-ft radius around it make a Dexterity save. If no one holds the Pilot role, the save automatically fails. A target takes 8d6 mega Bludgeoning damage on a failure, or half on a success." + HL + "With a slot of 4th level or higher, the damage rises by 1d6 mega for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Orbital Hardlight Cannon": ["500 ft, up to 3 rounds, Concentration. A 1 mile high, 15 ft radius beam deals 20d10 Radiant and moves 60 ft a turn.",
 "500 ft, up to 3 rounds, Concentration. You gather an aurora of light into a huge hardlight construct, an orbital cannon 1 mile above you. It fires a blinding beam into a cylinder 15 ft in radius and 1 mile high, centered on a point in range. When a creature enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it makes a Dexterity save and takes 20d10 Radiant damage on a failure, or half on a success. The beam ignites flammable nonmagical objects in the area that are not worn or carried. On each of your turns after casting, you can use an action to move the beam up to 60 ft in any direction."],
"Paradox": ["60 ft. Undo one action taken in range within the last round, and its actor takes 10d8 Psychic.",
 "60 ft. You twist time into knots and undo one action of your choice, taken within range in the last round. Reality recoils from the damage. The direct effects of the action, such as damage from an attack or spell, are undone. Indirect effects, such as creatures choosing to move elsewhere, are not. The creature that took the action takes 10d8 Psychic damage as its history is rewritten."],
"Perception Hack": ["15 ft, Concentration. Up to five willing creatures become silent and invisible to constructs.",
 "15 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You filter your presence from the minds of machines. Choose up to five willing creatures in range. They become silent and invisible to constructs. The spell ends for a target that attacks or casts a spell. A living construct, such as a vect, that would see or hear you can make a Wisdom save to resist."],
"Perforating Smite": ["Self, Concentration. Your next blaster shot becomes a 5 ft line, Dexterity save for the weapon's damage.",
 "Self, bonus action, up to 1 minute, Concentration. The next time you attack with a blaster before the spell ends, the shot is charged with huge power. Instead of an attack roll against one target, the shot becomes a line 5 ft wide from you out to the weapon's normal range. Each creature in the line makes a Dexterity save and takes the weapon's normal damage on a failure, or half on a success."],
"Polybrachia": ["Touch, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. A creature gains two extra spectral arms that hold items and give an extra melee attack.",
 "Touch, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Two muscular arms of arcane energy appear on a creature you touch. They work fully and can hold weapons and shields (so 2 two-handed weapons or 4 one-handed weapons), make somatic components and do other tasks, but they grant no extra actions. For the duration the target has Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made with the extra arms. If the arms carry weapons, the target can use a bonus action to make an extra melee weapon attack with them."],
"Psychedelics": ["60 ft, 1 hour. Recolor creatures and objects you choose, and Dexterity save or Disadvantage on attacks for a turn.",
 "60 ft, 1 hour. The colors around you swirl in a rainbow before settling far from their originals. The colors of all creatures and objects you choose in range change randomly and stay brightly unnatural for the duration. Each affected creature you choose also makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it has Disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn."],
"Repulsor Ring": ["5 ft, Concentration. A 5 ft ward: only chosen creatures enter, ranged attacks inside have Disadvantage, melee attackers are pushed 10 ft.",
 "5 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You outline a 5-ft-diameter circle on the ground, warded against intruders. Only creatures you choose can step inside. Any ranged attack roll against a target in the circle has Disadvantage. If a hostile creature makes a melee attack against a target in the circle, the attacker is pushed back 10 ft right after the attack."],
"Rift": ["10,000 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Ten 200 ft panels form an impassable wall that can become permanent.",
 "10,000 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. You tear a rift in space at a point in range. It is made of 10 panels, each 200 ft long, 200 ft wide and 25 ft thick, arranged as you like so long as each panel touches another and they form one continuous wall. You cannot place a panel in a space with a creature or object. The rift is impassable and blocks line of sight. It counts as an object with AC 15 and 90 mega hit points, and the spell ends if it drops to 0. If you keep Concentration for the full duration, the rift becomes permanent, though it can still be dispelled or destroyed. Otherwise it vanishes when the spell ends." + HL + "With a slot of 3rd level or higher, the rift gains 5 panels for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Scramble Targeting": ["5,000 ft, Concentration. A ship's gunners have Disadvantage on ship gun attacks unless they save.",
 "5,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Choose a spaceship you see in range. Its gunners each make a Wisdom save. On a failure, a gunner has Disadvantage on all attack rolls with ship-mounted guns for the duration. A gunner who is not incapacitated can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on themself on a success."],
"Simulation": ["Self, 1 minute. The GM summarizes the likely events of the next 24 hours.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You run a full digital simulation of the next day's events and gain insight into a probable future. The GM summarizes the likely events of the next 24 hours. You set the parameters from what you know, so the summary does not include unknown facts, such as an ambush or a traitor in your midst, or unlikely events, such as gaining or losing a companion."],
"Spacetime Distortion": ["120 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Warp distance around a creature so close creatures count as farther and the reverse.",
 "120 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. You warp spacetime around a creature you see in range. An unwilling creature makes a Constitution save to resist. Creatures within 5 ft of the target count as 10 ft away, and creatures 10 ft away count as 5 ft away. Other creatures can move through the target's space if they do not end there." + HL + "With a slot of 4th level or higher, you can distort space far more. Creatures 5 ft from the target count as 60 ft away, those 10 ft away count as 5 ft away, and those 15 ft away count as 10 ft away. Ranged attacks against the target have Disadvantage."],
"Splice": ["60 ft, 1 hour. Copy movement, resistances, senses or a trait from a creature, even a dead one, onto a touched recipient.",
 "60 ft, 1 hour. A special glass syringe worth 1,000 gp is needed. With a pinprick beam of arcana, you take a genetic sample from a creature you see in range and give it to a recipient you touch. The donor need not be alive or whole, as long as you target part of a creature that died in the last 10 days. The recipient gains one of these from the donor, your choice: its speed and movement types; all its damage resistances; its special senses; or one special trait, such as a ghast's Stench. If you pick a trait, the GM decides which one, if any. The recipient gains nothing that is not a racial or monster statistic. Its appearance shifts to a hybrid of the donor and itself. These changes and gained traits last for the duration."],
"Technical Difficulties": ["60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. A piece of magical technology malfunctions and cannot be used.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Lights flicker, blasters misfire and arcane terminals crash. Choose a piece of magical technology in range. It malfunctions unpredictably and cannot be used for the duration."],
"Technomancy": ["60 ft. Perform a basic operation on a device you see, like pressing a button or entering keystrokes.",
 "60 ft, bonus action. With a complex input gesture, you manipulate a device you see in range. You can perform any basic operation, such as pressing an external button, entering a dozen keystrokes, doing an authorized operation like opening an unlocked door, dimming or brightening a screen or muting a speaker. You cannot disconnect or reconnect wires, or do an unauthorized operation like crashing a device or changing its password without knowing the old one."],
"Telaros's Speedcycle": ["30 ft. A Large two-wheeled vehicle, speed 100 ft, leaves a 10 ft force wall behind it.",
 "30 ft, 1 minute. A Large two-wheeled vehicle with holographic circuits appears in an unoccupied space in range. It has AC 10 and 10 hit points, and roars to life when its controls are grasped. For the duration you or a creature you choose can operate it, and one creature can ride as a passenger. It has a speed of 100 ft and covers 10 miles in an hour. Wherever it moves it leaves a bright, translucent wall of force 10 ft high that nothing can pass. The wall is immune to all damage, but a 20-ft section can be destroyed by dispel magic or disintegrate. Wall sections the rider creates vanish at the end of the rider's next turn. The spell ends if you dismiss it with an action, if the cycle drops to 0 hit points, or if it hits its own walls or another solid obstacle. The walls vanish when it ends. If it ends from damage or a collision, the rider and passenger fall Prone."],
"Telaros's Terrific Transport": ["Touch. A Huge shuttle carries a pilot, eight passengers and 2,000 lb, and can reach space.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. A Huge shuttle with glowing holographic circuits appears before you. It holds 9 Medium creatures (a pilot and eight passengers) and 2,000 lb of cargo, and is enclosed with clean, breathable air. It flies at 100 ft per round, or 1,500 ft per round in a vacuum. It can reach space on most planets by flying straight up for 5 minutes, and enter an atmosphere by descending for the same time. It has life support and sensors, and can dock with larger ships like a fighter-sized ship. It has AC 10 and 8 mega hit points, and the spell ends if it drops to 0. When the spell ends, the shuttle sets down gently if a substantial planetoid is nearby, giving passengers time to leave."],
"Turbulence": ["10,000 ft, Concentration. A ship's speed is halved if its pilot fails a Dexterity save.",
 "10,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Choose a spaceship you see in range. Its pilot makes a Dexterity save. On a failure the ship's speed is halved for the duration. A pilot who is not incapacitated can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success."],
"Voidlight": ["120 ft. Constitution save or 1d8 Radiant, and 8s on damage dice explode.",
 "120 ft. For an instant you open a portal into the Void and show the hideous lights beyond. Choose a creature you see. It makes a Constitution save, with Advantage if it cannot see you. On a failure it takes 1d8 Radiant damage. If you roll an 8 on any damage die, you can roll an extra d8 and add it, rolling again on another 8, and so on. You can roll a total number of damage dice for this cantrip equal to twice the dice you first rolled.\nThe damage rises by 1d8 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
}
